Hi,

I thought the people here might be interested in a new game I've just completed.
The website is www.lostinflatspace.com

Flatspace is a space trading and flight simulation that has elements of Elite
and rogue-like games, and in particular my favourites Nethack and ADOM. The game
is fully 3D and has a top down, Asteroids style viewpoint.

The game has most of the Elite-like features of Frontier: Elite 2 and a little
bit more. Cargo has sub classes. The combat is more arcade like while retaining
many simulation elements. Your multi-skilled crew can be assigned to different
roles, and people can be captured alive from other ships. Mining, bounty hunting
and mission roles are interesting and viable alternatives to trading. Ships and
stations can have gun turrets, and carry fighter craft. Asteroid fields are
dense, and smoky nebula can fill sectors. There is an arcade subgame too, for
combat practise.

Rogue like elements also add the the unique appeal of the game. The galaxy map
starts unexplored and must be revealed. You get a choice of character, and many
random options like the ability to play in a random or seeded universe. A
graveyard shows your past games, and you can optionally choose to renage on
save-game cheating. There is a quest object, a galactic hyperdrive.

There are several hundred ship upgrades, including over 20 different types of
missiles, and lots of counter measures than just flares. Weapons include machine
guns, lasers and even flame throwers. Robot crew members, scanners and tractor
beams of all sorts, and even pets and luxury items for the rich and successful.

For more information, screenshots, and the demo visit www.lostinflatspace.com.
The manual is online there too if you want more detail. I've been working on
this game for most of this year. Thanks for reading.

